      "body": "## Motivation\n\nAt the end of the weight load, the ranks wait for each other in a barrier with a fixed 480 s timeout (`UNBALANCED_MODEL_LOADING_TIMEOUT_S`). With KTransformers the ranks load very different amounts: rank 0 also builds the CPU experts. For DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash-1017 on 2x RTX 5070 Ti, rank 0's extra work takes well over 480 s when the checkpoint is read from disk. The other rank's barrier then times out and a TP2 launch fails. Our launches set 1800 s.\n\n## Modifications\n\n- `python/sglang/srt/environ.py`: `SGLANG_UNBALANCED_LOAD_TIMEOUT_S = EnvInt(480)`.\n- `load_model_utils.py`: the barrier timeout reads it. The default is 480 s, as before.\n\n## Accuracy Tests\n\nNot affected.\n\n## Speed Tests and Profiling\n\nNot affected.\n\n## Checklist\n\n- [x] Format your code according to the [Format code with pre-commit](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#format-code-with-pre-commit).\n- [ ] Add unit tests according to the [Run and add unit tests](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#run-and-add-unit-tests).\n- [ ] Update documentation according to [Write documentations](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#write-documentations).\n- [ ] Provide accuracy and speed benchmark results according to [Test the accuracy](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#test-the-accuracy) and [Benchmark the speed](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#benchmark-the-speed).\n- [x] Follow the SGLang code style [guidance](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#code-style-guidance).\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01C2UBZdnrDZSBh8yQz8rc9g\n\n<!-- pr-states:start -->\n---\n### CI States\n\nLatest PR Test (Base): <!-- slot:pr-test:start -->:x: [Run #39262920524](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/39262920524)<!-- slot:pr-test:end -->\